---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const b='/equipment/10-06/',vendor='https://www.sutter.com/micropipette/p-1000',cover='https://www.sutter.com/hubfs/WEB%20-%20Manuals/P-1000_OpMan.pdf#page=1';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Sutter P-1000 non-operational inspection display" description="Inspect a metric shell and check fit of an oversized inert rod in a fictional geometry gauge." wide={true}><article class="equipment" id="sutter"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/10-06/">← Equipment 10-06</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#sut-evidence">Evidence</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">10-06 / NON-OPERATIONAL DISPLAY</p><h2>Two bands, one inert gauge rod</h2><p class="eq-lede">Lift the model cover and compare the solid teaching rod with two fictional gauge bands. Centering a 120 × 6 mm rod gives 14 mm overlap on both sides. No real machine operation or fabrication is represented.</p></header>
<div class="g-cols"><section><h3>Sutter Instrument P-1000</h3><canvas id="sut-model" aria-label="Orbitable P-1000 shell, cover and inert rod gauge"></canvas><p id="sut-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="sut-front">Whole station / reset view</button><button id="sut-gauge">Gauge-band close-up</button><button id="sut-rear">Rear view</button><p>The model handle hinges the visual cover. The silver bands only calculate geometric fit. All front controls are decorative.</p></section>
<section><h3>Dry geometry only</h3><label>Oversized solid rod length<select id="sut-length"><option value="120">120 mm</option><option value="100">100 mm</option><option value="140">140 mm</option></select></label><label>Fictional rod diameter<select id="sut-diam"><option value="6">6 mm</option><option value="4">4 mm</option><option value="8">8 mm</option></select></label><label>Rod center offset, mm<input id="sut-center" type="number" min="-16" max="16" step="any" value="0"/></label><button id="sut-cover">Open visual cover</button><button id="sut-check">Check geometric fit</button><button id="sut-reset">Restore display</button><p id="sut-status" role="status"></p><p id="sut-read"></p><button id="sut-export">Download passive inspection JSON</button><p><a href={b+'example-fit.json'}>Example report</a>. Record includes the rod span, known gauge bands and a diametrical margin. No fabricated output, glass or electrical result.</p></section></div>
<section id="sut-evidence"><h3>Visual evidence and checks</h3><p>Original P-1000 geometry based on the <a href={cover}>Sutter Rev. 3.07 cover photograph</a> and the <a href={vendor}>product envelope</a> (nominal 530 × 300 × 360 mm, width × height × depth). The base is source-scaled; face, cover movement, inactive parts and rods are authored approximations. The dry insert deliberately replaces any actual working geometry, and the model omits powered apparatus.</p><div class="g-cols"><figure><img src={b+'station.webp'} alt="Original render of Sutter P-1000 instrument shell"/><figcaption>Original closed exterior: fascia, cover, dark control face and adjustment shapes.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={b+'gauge.webp'} alt="Original inert surrogate rod supported by two schematic bands"/><figcaption>Original open-cover dry insert. These dimensions and positions are not characteristics of a real specimen or mechanism.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>The two fictional bands span [−55,−41] and [41,55] mm along the rod. A positive geometric result requires at least 8 mm overlap at each band and a diameter no larger than 7 mm. Calculating the intersection of intervals cannot predict seating force, actual working clearance or instrument behavior.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Independent case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>120 × 6 mm centered</td><td>14/14 mm, +1 mm margin</td><td>14/14, +1; fits</td></tr><tr><td>100 mm long, +12 mm shift</td><td>Left 0 mm; right 14 mm</td><td>0/14; does not fit</td></tr><tr><td>8 mm diameter</td><td>−1 mm margin</td><td>−1; does not fit</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href={b+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={b+'p1000.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={b+'dry-gauges.mjs'}>Pure dry fit and state actions</a> · <a href={b+'vr.json'}>VR targets and presentation hinge</a>. No headset or hardware verification claimed.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/10-06/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>#sutter .g-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#sutter section{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);margin:1rem 0;min-width:0}#sutter :is(input,select,button){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.45rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}#sutter label{display:grid;gap:.2rem;min-width:0;margin:.35rem 0}#sutter label :is(input,select){width:100%;min-width:0}#sutter button{margin:.35rem .25rem .2rem 0;cursor:pointer}#sutter button:disabled{opacity:.5}#sutter button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b28d5e}#sut-model{display:block;width:100%;height:335px;touch-action:none}#sutter figure{margin:.5rem 0}#sutter figure img{width:100%}#sutter table{font-size:.9rem;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;text-align:left}#sutter td,#sutter th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}@media(max-width:780px){#sutter .g-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#sut-model{height:282px}}</style>
